## Context: V3.6.0.7 spike that motivated D6

V3.6.0.7 D6 profiling spike (`3e1e4deff50` + `docs/audits/2026-05-25-phase-5-7-v3-6-0-7-spike.md`) measured `workbookSnapshot` median cost at 100k cells / 50% format = **251.38 ms** (5× the 50 ms threshold).  rebuild_workbook + sheet/table/column rename-repair walks dominate; D4 format::render adds ~99 ms on top.  V3.6.0.8 D6 ships incremental deltas to skip these costs in steady-state IDE editing.

## What V3.6.0.8 ships across the 3-commit chain

### V3.6.0.8.1 (`ebe7c946429`, docs-only)

Locked the design.  Three-option evaluation:
- (a) Cache rebuilt+repaired Workbook + clone-and-apply-delta -- **CHOSEN**.
- (b) Read from `last_snapshot` cache + skip `rebuild_workbook` -- **REJECTED** because `last_snapshot.formula` carries pre-rename-repair text (would silently regress V3.5.0.X A-HIGH-2 contract: workbookSnapshot surfaces REPAIRED formula text post `repair_sheet_rename_chain` + `repair_table_rename_chain` + `repair_column_rename_chain`).
- (c) Hybrid revalidate-changed-cells -- **DEFERRED to V3.7+**.

8-step algorithm + 4 invalidation triggers + 5 new risks R-V3.6-14..18 documented in `.plans/_active.md` + `docs/architecture/ide-consumer-contract.md § 4.1.z6`.

