-only fast-path is steady-state IDE-editing happy path; any `Op::RenameSheet | RenameTable | RenameColumn` in the delta triggers full rebuild_workbook + repair walks (because repair touches ALL formula cells in the workbook, not just the renamed sheet -- verified at `crates/ql-collab/src/repair.rs:227-345`).  Locked invalidation triggers: `merge_bytes` + `discard_pending_ops` + `undo` + `redo` all call new `force_clear_workbook_cache()` helper; `append_op` does NOT invalidate (it's the cell-only fast-path target).  5 new risks documented R-V3.6-14..18 (cached-Workbook-stale-after-Loro-retract; VV-vs-op_count-drift; multi-peer-concurrent-rename-cell-edit; Workbook-clone-cost-may-exceed-20ms-at-100k-fallback-to-Arc-COW; apply_op-private-to-ql-oplog-prefer-new-`apply_ops_in_range(from, to)`-public-helper-on-OpLog).  R-V3.6-NEW (from V3.6.0.7 spike) closed as CLOSED-AT-V3.6.0.8.1.  Sub-step rollout: V3.6.0.8.1 ✅ docs-only lock; V3.6.0.8.2 = engine PART 1 (new fields + `force_clear_workbook_cache` + invalidation wiring at 4 callsites + new `apply_ops_in_range` helper on `OpLog` + ql-collab regression tests); V3.6.0.8.3 = engine PART 2 (`workbook_snapshot_delta` napi method + cell-only fast-path + rename-full-rebuild branch + staleness check + bench delta vs full snapshot at 100k cells + napi shape tests); V3.6.0.8.4 = V3.6.0.X audit-of-D6 (parallel Codex Lane A + Opus Lane B + closures).  D6 total arc estimate: 4 cycles across ≥2 sessions.  Files modified at V3.6.0.8.1: `.plans/_active.md` (V3.6.0.8.1 SHIPPED sub-section + frontmatter + R-V3.6-14..18 + R-V3.6-NEW resolution); this file (this paragraph); `docs/architecture/ide-consumer-contract.md § 4.1.z6` (D6 row + V3.6.0.8.1 sub-section preview with napi shape + IDE consumer protocol).  No engine source touched.  No new tests.  No IDE / mocha changes.  Tests baselines unchanged: ql-collab **136/136** + ql-oplog **67/67** + ql-collab-ws 40/40 (+2 ignored doctests) + IDE mocha **384/384**.  This session counted **1 plan-implement-audit cycle** (V3.6.0.8.1 docs lock), WITHIN the CLAUDE.md ≤2 cycle ceiling.
docs/MASTER-PLAN.md:564:✅ **V3.6.0.8.2 D6 ENGINE PART 1 SHIPPED** at engine (this commit) (2026-05-25).  Lands the engine-side foundation for the V3.6.0.8.3 napi `workbook_snapshot_delta` per the V3.6.0.8.1 design lock; no new napi surface yet.  Two new fields on `CollabSession` -- `last_snapshot_workbook: Option<Arc<Workbook>>` (post-repair) + `last_snapshot_oplog_vv: Option<loro::VersionVector>` -- with `pub fn` accessors (`last_snapshot_workbook` / `last_snapshot_oplog_vv`) + setter (`set_workbook_cache(Arc<Workbook>, VersionVector)`) + invalidator (`force_clear_workbook_cache()` -- production, not test-gated).  Both fields default `None` in both `new` + `from_snapshot` constructors (per V3.6.0.8.1 lock: `from_snapshot` does NOT pre-populate the cache because rebuild_workbook + repair walks cost more than waiting until a consumer needs the result).  Invalidation wired at 4 production callsites: (1) `merge_bytes` (after rebuild_snapshot_cache; remote ops may shift LWW winners), (2) `discard_pending_ops` (after rebuild_snapshot_cache; fork_at_vv dropped ops), (3) `undo` (AT TOP, BEFORE Loro's undo per R-V3.6-14 -- retract may have included rename op whose effect would need un-repair), (4) `redo` (AT TOP, mirror of undo).  `append_op` does NOT invalidate (cell-only fast-path target; explicitly verified by `v3_6_0_8_2_append_op_does_NOT_invalidate_workbook_cache` regression test).  New public free function in ql-oplog: `pub fn apply_ops_in_range(log, workbook, from_index, to_index, registry) -> Result<usize, ReplayError>` (re-exported via `ql_oplog::apply_ops_in_range`; iterates `log.iter().skip(from).take(to-from)` and invokes the existing private `apply_op` per op; preserves `replay_into`'s from-empty contract; out-of-range to_index silently stops at log end; empty/inverted range = O(1) no-op returning 0).  V3.6.0.8.3 napi `workbook_snapshot_delta` will use this for the cell-only fast-path delta replay onto the cached Workbook clone.  `force_clear_snapshot_cache` test seam extended to clear the workbook cache too (cohesive test-state discipline).  +13 ql-collab regression tests (149/149 pass; +13 over V3.6.0.X audit-of-D5 136 baseline): 8 workbook cache invariants (fresh/from_snapshot empty; set populates atomic; force_clear resets atomic; merge_bytes/discard/undo/redo invalidate; append_op preserves; Arc identity preserved through setter) + 4 apply_ops_in_range correctness (empty noop; full-range matches replay_into; forward-from-partial composes correctly; oversized to_index saturates at log end) + 1 cache discipline (Arc ptr_eq through setter).  No new napi (V3.6.0.8.3 scope); no IDE / mocha changes (mocha baseline 384/384 unchanged); engine workspace release build clean.  Rule 4 arc terminus HELD at 6 (per the V3.6.0.8.1 lock: Workbook auto-derives Send+Sync via field composition at `crates/ql-storage/src/workbook.rs:295-299`; Arc<T>: Send+Sync iff T; VersionVector via Loro's BTreeMap<PeerID, Counter>; Option<X>: Send+Sync iff X; 0 new triggers).  R-V3.6-14 (cached Workbook stale after Loro retract) CLOSURE LANDED via the undo + redo top-of-method clear discipline.  R-V3.6-15 (VV vs op_count drift) debug-assert deferred to V3.6.0.8.3 -- the invariant is "set together / clear together" not "monotonic drift" at this layer.  R-V3.6-17 (Workbook clone cost) profiled at V3.6.0.8.3.  R-V3.6-18 (apply_op private) CLOSED via the new `apply_ops_in_range` public helper.  This session counted **2 plan-implement-audit cycles** (V3.6.0.8.1 docs lock + V3.6.0.8.2 engine PART 1), AT the CLAUDE.md ≤2 cycle ceiling.
docs/MASTER-PLAN.md:566:✅ **V3.6.0.8.3 D6 ENGINE PART 2 napi SHIPPED** at engine (this commit) + IDE (this commit) (2026-05-25; user-directed cycle-3 override of the CLAUDE.md ≤2 cycle ceiling).  Lands the napi surface for incremental WorkbookSnapshot deltas per the V3.6.0.8.1 design lock.  New `WorkbookSnapshotDeltaJson` napi struct (`changedCells: Vec<ChangedCellJson>` + `removedCells: Vec<RemovedCellJson>` + `sheetsChanged: Vec<SheetSnapshotJson>` + `sheetsRemoved: Vec<u32>` + `formatsAdded: Vec<FormatDefJson>` + `version: Buffer` + `fullRebuildRequired: bool`) + 2 helper structs `ChangedCellJson { sheet, cell: CellSnapshotJson }` + `RemovedCellJson { sheet, row, col }`.  New `#[napi(js_name = "workbookSnapshotDelta")] CollabSession::workbookSnapshotDelta(lastSeenVersion: Buffer)` method implementing the V3.6.0.8.1 8-step algorithm: cache-miss + decode-VV + staleness + same-VV-fast-path + op-enumeration + rename-detection + cell-only-fast-path (Arc-deref-clone + ql_oplog::apply_ops_in_range + skip repair walks) + JSON-delta-build.  Rename ops trigger fullRebuild fallback (locked at V3.6.0.8.1 -- the rename delta would degenerate to "all cells with formulas" anyway).  Existing `workbookSnapshot` napi now populates the cache via `set_workbook_cache(Arc::clone(&workbook), oplog_vv())` after `rebuild_workbook`; `workbook` wrapped in `Arc` BEFORE rendering so no double-clone (rendering reads through Arc::deref).  Added `last_snapshot_op_count: Option<usize>` 3rd cache field (revision to V3.6.0.8.2's 2-field cache invariants -- delta path derives the replay slice `[op_count, log.len())` without a VV->op_count walk; preserves the "all Some / all None" invariant); extended `set_workbook_cache` (pins op_count alongside VV) + `force_clear_workbook_cache` (clears all 3 fields) + new `last_snapshot_op_count()` accessor.  New `pub fn oplog_vv(&self)` + `pub fn log(&self) -> &OpLog` accessors on `CollabSession` so the napi can grab the VV at populate time + enumerate ops at delta time.  `loro::VersionVector` re-exported as `ql_oplog::VersionVector` for ergonomics (avoids a direct loro dep on ql-bindings-node).  New free fns `empty_delta` + `classify_delta_op` at file scope (helpers; `classify_delta_op` recurses into `Op::BatchCommit` mirroring V3.4.0.X HIGH-1 walker discipline).  IDE: types.ts adds `WorkbookSnapshotDeltaJson` + `ChangedCellJson` + `RemovedCellJson` interfaces + `CollabSessionInstance.workbookSnapshotDelta(lastSeenVersion: Buffer): WorkbookSnapshotDeltaJson` method.  +6 mocha shape tests (390/390 pass; +6 over V3.6.0.X audit-of-D5 live 384 baseline -- the 381 documented baseline was a 3-count undercount): empty Buffer + no-cache + same-VV fast-path + cell-only emits changes + rename triggers fullRebuild + undo invalidates cache.  Tests: ql-collab 149/149 unchanged (V3.6.0.8.2 baseline preserved; new op_count field naturally pinned by existing set_workbook_cache test calls) + ql-oplog 67/67 + IDE mocha **390/390** + engine workspace release build clean.  Rule 4 arc terminus HELD at 6 (all new napi struct fields + 1 new `last_snapshot_op_count: Option<usize>` cache field are positive Send+Sync composition; 0 new triggers).  V3.6.0.8.3 scope limitations: `removedCells` always empty (V3.7+); `sheetsChanged` always empty in cell-only path (cell ops don't change sheet metadata; full-rebuild paths return `fullRebuildRequired=true` instead); rename ops trigger fullRebuild rather than incremental rename delta.  Bench delta-vs-full at 100k cells DEFERRED to V3.6.0.8.4 audit-of-D6 (functional + regression test surface is complete at V3.6.0.8.3; perf verification + R-V3.6-15 full debug-assert + R-V3.6-17 clone-cost profile all naturally fit into V3.6.0.8.4's audit cycle).  This session counted **3 plan-implement-audit cycles** (V3.6.0.8.1 docs lock + V3.6.0.8.2 engine PART 1 + V3.6.0.8.3 napi), 1 over the CLAUDE.md ≤2 cycle ceiling; **user-directed exception** via AskUserQuestion at cycle 3 entry.
