.plans/_active.md:299:   - **V3.6.0.8.1 -- DESIGN LOCK** ✅ SHIPPED at engine (this commit) (2026-05-25).  Docs-only lock; no engine source modified.  Mirrors V3.6.0.1 pattern.  Resolves the open R-V3.6-NEW question from V3.6.0.7 spike: **option (a) cache rebuilt+repaired Workbook + clone-and-apply-delta is CHOSEN**.  Option (b) read-from-`last_snapshot`-and-skip-rebuild_workbook is INFEASIBLE because `last_snapshot.formula` carries PRE-rename-repair text (would silently regress the V3.5.0.X A-HIGH-2 contract that `workbookSnapshot` surfaces REPAIRED formula text); option (c) hybrid revalidate-changed-cells deferred to V3.7+.  Locked napi surface: new `workbookSnapshotDelta(lastSeenVersion: Buffer) -> WorkbookSnapshotDeltaJson` method + new `WorkbookSnapshotDeltaJson { changedCells, removedCells, sheetsChanged, sheetsRemoved, formatsAdded, version, fullRebuildRequired }`.  Two-call discipline: empty `lastSeenVersion` Buffer (or unknown VV) returns `fullRebuildRequired=true`; IDE then calls `workbookSnapshot()` and caches the `version` token for subsequent delta calls.  Locked internal state: 2 new fields on `CollabSession` -- `last_snapshot_workbook: Option<Arc<Workbook>>` (post-repair) + `last_snapshot_oplog_vv: Option<VersionVector>`.  Both positive Send+Sync compositionally (Workbook auto-derives via field composition per `crates/ql-storage/src/workbook.rs:295-299`; Arc<T>: Send+Sync iff T; VersionVector via Loro's BTreeMap<PeerID, Counter>).  **Rule 4 arc terminus stays at 6**.  Locked algorithm: 8-step body -- cache-miss + decode-VV + staleness-check + same-VV fast-path + op-enumeration-since-cached-VV + rename-detection + cell-only fast-path (clone Arc::make_mut + apply per-op + skip repair) OR rename-full-rebuild branch + JSON-delta-build.  Cell-only fast-path is the steady-state IDE-editing happy path; rename ops trigger full rebuild_workbook + repair walks (because repair touches ALL formula cells, not just renamed sheet).  Locked invalidation triggers: `merge_bytes` + `discard_pending_ops` + `undo` + `redo` all call new `force_clear_workbook_cache()` helper; `append_op` does NOT invalidate (it's the cell-only fast-path target).  5 new risks documented R-V3.6-14..18 (cached-Workbook-stale-after-retract; VV-vs-op_count-drift; multi-peer-concurrent-rename-cell-edit; Workbook-clone-cost-may-exceed-20ms-at-100k; apply_op-private-to-ql-oplog).  R-V3.6-NEW (from V3.6.0.7) closed by this lock; renamed inline below to R-V3.6-NEW → CLOSED-AT-V3.6.0.8.1.  Sub-step rollout: V3.6.0.8.1 ✅ docs lock; V3.6.0.8.2 = engine PART 1 (new fields + force_clear_workbook_cache + invalidation wiring + new `apply_ops_in_range` helper on OpLog + ql-collab regression tests); V3.6.0.8.3 = engine PART 2 (`workbook_snapshot_delta` napi + bench delta vs full snapshot at 100k cells + napi shape tests); V3.6.0.8.4 = V3.6.0.X audit-of-D6 (parallel Codex Lane A + Opus Lane B + closures).  See `docs/architecture/ide-consumer-contract.md § 4.1.z6` for the consumer-facing mirror.  Cycle count for this session: 1 (V3.6.0.8.1 lock only); within CLAUDE.md ≤2 ceiling.
.plans/_active.md:300:   - **V3.6.0.8.2 -- ENGINE PART 1** ✅ SHIPPED at engine (this commit) (2026-05-25).  New `last_snapshot_workbook: Option<Arc<Workbook>>` + `last_snapshot_oplog_vv: Option<loro::VersionVector>` fields on `CollabSession` (initialized `None` in both `new` + `from_snapshot`).  New `pub fn force_clear_workbook_cache(&mut self)` helper (resets both fields atomically, preserving "Some iff Some" invariant).  New `pub fn set_workbook_cache(&mut self, Arc<Workbook>, VersionVector)` for V3.6.0.8.3 napi to populate post-`rebuild_workbook`.  New `pub fn last_snapshot_workbook(&self)` + `pub fn last_snapshot_oplog_vv(&self)` read accessors.  Invalidation wired at 4 production callsites: `merge_bytes` (after `rebuild_snapshot_cache`), `discard_pending_ops` (after `rebuild_snapshot_cache`), `undo` (at top, BEFORE Loro's undo per R-V3.6-14), `redo` (at top, mirror of undo).  Append-op does NOT invalidate (cell-only fast-path target; verified by regression test).  New `pub fn apply_ops_in_range(log, workbook, from, to, registry) -> Result<usize, ReplayError>` free function in `ql-oplog::replay` (re-exported via `ql_oplog::apply_ops_in_range`; preserves `replay_into`'s from-empty contract; out-of-range to_index silently stops at log end; empty range = O(1) no-op).  Also extended `force_clear_snapshot_cache` test seam to clear workbook cache for cohesive test-state.  +13 ql-collab regression tests (149/149 pass): `v3_6_0_8_2_fresh_session_has_empty_workbook_cache` + `..._from_snapshot_has_empty_workbook_cache` + `..._set_workbook_cache_populates_both_fields` + `..._force_clear_workbook_cache_resets_both_fields` + `..._merge_bytes_invalidates_workbook_cache` + `..._discard_pending_ops_invalidates_workbook_cache` + `..._undo_invalidates_workbook_cache` + `..._redo_invalidates_workbook_cache` + `..._append_op_does_NOT_invalidate_workbook_cache` + `..._apply_ops_in_range_empty_is_noop` + `..._apply_ops_in_range_full_matches_replay_into` + `..._apply_ops_in_range_forward_from_partial` + `..._apply_ops_in_range_oversized_to_index_silently_stops_at_log_end`.  Rule 4 arc terminus HELD at 6 (positive Send+Sync composition on the 2 new field types per the V3.6.0.8.1 lock; 0 new triggers).  No new napi surface; no IDE / mocha changes.  Tests: ql-collab **149/149** + ql-oplog **67/67** + ql-collab-ws **40/40** (+2 ignored doctests) + IDE mocha **384/384** unchanged + engine workspace release build clean.
.plans/_active.md:301:   - **V3.6.0.8.3 -- ENGINE PART 2 napi** ✅ SHIPPED at engine (this commit) + IDE (this commit) (2026-05-25).  napi surface: new `WorkbookSnapshotDeltaJson { changedCells, removedCells, sheetsChanged, sheetsRemoved, formatsAdded, version: Buffer, fullRebuildRequired: bool }` napi struct + new `ChangedCellJson { sheet, cell: CellSnapshotJson }` + new `RemovedCellJson { sheet, row, col }` napi helper structs.  New `#[napi] CollabSession::workbookSnapshotDelta(lastSeenVersion: Buffer)` method.  Cache populated in existing `workbookSnapshot` napi via `set_workbook_cache(Arc::clone(&workbook), oplog_vv())` after `rebuild_workbook`; `workbook` wrapped in `Arc` BEFORE rendering so no double-clone.  Algorithm follows the V3.6.0.8.1 lock's 8 steps: cache-miss + decode-VV + staleness + same-VV-fast-path + op-enumeration + rename-detection + cell-only-fast-path (Arc-deref-clone + `ql_oplog::apply_ops_in_range` + skip repair walks) + JSON-delta-build (rename branch returns `fullRebuildRequired=true`).  V3.6.0.8.3 scope limitations: `removedCells` always empty (V3.7+); `sheetsChanged` always empty in cell-only path (cell ops don't change sheet metadata); rename ops trigger full-rebuild fallback rather than incremental rename delta.  Added `last_snapshot_op_count: Option<usize>` 3rd cache field (revision to V3.6.0.8.2 cache invariants) so delta path derives the replay slice `[op_count, log.len())` without VV->op_count walk -- the three-field "set together / clear together" invariant preserves.  New accessor `pub fn last_snapshot_op_count() -> Option<usize>` + extended `set_workbook_cache` (pins op_count alongside VV) + extended `force_clear_workbook_cache` (clears all 3 fields).  New `pub fn oplog_vv(&self) -> VersionVector` + `pub fn log(&self) -> &OpLog` accessors on `CollabSession` so the napi (outside ql-collab) can grab the VV at populate time + enumerate ops at delta time.  `loro::VersionVector` re-exported as `ql_oplog::VersionVector` for downstream-crate ergonomics (avoids a direct `loro` dep on ql-bindings-node).  New free fns `empty_delta(version, full_rebuild_required)` + `classify_delta_op(op, has_rename, changed_cells, removed_sheets, new_formats)` at file scope (helpers for the algorithm; `classify_delta_op` recurses into `Op::BatchCommit` mirroring V3.4.0.X HIGH-1 walker discipline).  IDE: `types.ts` interfaces extended (`CollabSessionInstance.workbookSnapshotDelta(lastSeenVersion: Buffer): WorkbookSnapshotDeltaJson` + new `WorkbookSnapshotDeltaJson` + `ChangedCellJson` + `RemovedCellJson` interfaces).  +6 mocha shape tests (390/390 pass; +6 over the V3.6.0.X audit-of-D5 live 384 baseline; the 381 documented baseline was a 3-count undercount from prior handoff): empty Buffer fullRebuild + no-cache fullRebuild + same-VV fast-path post workbookSnapshot + cell-only fast-path emits changed cells with deterministic sort + rename op triggers fullRebuild + undo invalidates cache.  ql-collab 149/149 unchanged + ql-oplog 67/67 unchanged + engine workspace release build clean.  Bench delta vs full at 100k cells DEFERRED to V3.6.0.8.4 (the audit-of-D6 cycle will naturally include the perf verification; functional + regression test surface is complete at V3.6.0.8.3).  R-V3.6-15 (VV vs op_count drift) PARTIAL closure: the three-field "all Some / all None" invariant is verified by the existing V3.6.0.8.2 regression tests + the new same-VV-fast-path test; full debug-assert on (log.len() == cached_op_count + ops_since) deferred to V3.6.0.8.4.  R-V3.6-17 (Workbook clone cost) profile deferred to V3.6.0.8.4.  Rule 4 arc terminus HELD at 6 (new fields + napi structs all positive Send+Sync composition; `ChangedCellJson` over `CellSnapshotJson` (existing) + `u32`; `RemovedCellJson` over 3 `u32`s; `WorkbookSnapshotDeltaJson` over `Vec<X>` for X each previously-walked + `Buffer` (Send+Sync via Vec<u8>) + `bool`; 0 new triggers).
.plans/_active.md:326:- **R-V3.6-14 Cached Workbook stale after Loro UndoManager retract.**  Loro's UndoManager retract COMPACTS the visible op log (R-V3.6-10 carry).  V3.6.0.8 cached Workbook would still reflect the pre-retract state -- a no-op for staleness if cell_op_index walks correctly, but a HARD STALENESS for rename ops that the retract un-did.  Mitigation: V3.6.0.8.2 `undo()` + `redo()` invocations call new `force_clear_workbook_cache()` BEFORE delegating to Loro's undo.  Mirrors the existing `force_clear_snapshot_cache` discipline at V3.6.0.4 D3.
.plans/_active.md:327:- **R-V3.6-15 VersionVector vs op_count drift.**  Loro's `oplog_vv()` returns a `BTreeMap<PeerID, Counter>` (per-peer counters), not a `usize` log length.  Cached `(VV, op_count)` pair COULD drift if `merge_bytes` advances VV without increasing local op_count (impossible? -- verify at V3.6.0.8.2 implementation), or if `undo` decrements VV (Loro VV is monotone -- undo adds a synthetic inverse op, never decrements).  Mitigation: V3.6.0.8.2 implementation adds a debug-assert that "VV at cache time matches the result of walking the log to op_count".  PARTIAL closure at V3.6.0.8.3: the three-field "all Some together / all None together" invariant is verified by V3.6.0.8.2 regression tests + the new V3.6.0.8.3 same-VV fast-path test (probe1.version == probe2's expected cached_vv).  Full debug-assert (`log.len() == cached_op_count + ops_since_cached_op_count`) deferred to V3.6.0.8.4 audit-of-D6.
.plans/_active.md:330:- **R-V3.6-18 `apply_op` is private to `ql-oplog`.**  D6 needs to apply single ops to an existing Workbook (the cell-only fast-path body).  Options at V3.6.0.8.2: (a) expose existing `apply_op` as `pub fn`, (b) add a new `apply_ops_in_range(log, workbook, from_index, to_index, registry) -> Result<usize, ReplayError>` helper on `OpLog` (preserves `replay_into`'s from-empty contract while giving D6 a clean public API).  **Decision: (b)**.  The new helper iterates `self.log.iter().enumerate().skip(from_index).take(to_index - from_index)` and invokes the existing private `apply_op` -- single public API + zero contract change for `replay_into`.
