docs/audits/2026-05-21-phase-5-5-v2-v3-step-1-codex.md:91:`self.log.oplog_vv()` clones an internal VV. How expensive is this? Looking at `loro::LoroDoc::oplog_vv`, it returns by value — does it clone N×u64 (one per peer) or something heavier? Under OnAppend per-keystroke, this fires on every mutation. Acceptable per-call cost?
docs/audits/2026-05-21-phase-5-5-v2-v3-step-1-codex.md:95:`merge_bytes` mutates `self.log` (adds peer ops) then calls `maybe_auto_flush`. Auto-flush calls `flush_delta_to_transport` which reads `self.log.oplog_vv()` (post-merge) and compares against `self.last_flushed_vv` (pre-merge). If the merge advanced the VV (peer had new ops), delta flush fires with `from = last_flushed_vv`. The delta bytes encode the ops added BY US PLUS the ops we merged FROM PEER.
