   118	/// which doesn't implement `Eq` (NaN != NaN).  Tests can still use
   119	/// `assert_eq!`; that calls `PartialEq::eq` which is fine for non-NaN
   120	/// numeric comparisons.  `FormatId` is `Eq` so doesn't change the
   121	/// CellState's PartialEq-only property.
   122	///
   123	/// ## V3.5.0.5 per-field LWW semantics (extends V3.4.0.2)
   124	///
   125	/// - `Op::PutValue` writes `state.value`, preserves `formula` + `format`.
   126	/// - `Op::PutFormula` writes `state.formula`, preserves `value` + `format`.
   127	/// - `Op::ClearFormula` clears `state.formula`, preserves `value` + `format`.
   128	/// - **`Op::SetCellFormat { id: Some(_) }` writes `state.format`, preserves
   129	///   `value` + `formula`** (V3.5.0.5 new).
   130	/// - **`Op::SetCellFormat { id: None }` clears `state.format`, preserves
   131	///   `value` + `formula`** (V3.5.0.5 new; the W5-80 "clear overlay" semantic).
   132	///
   133	/// A cell can carry ANY combination of (value, formula, format).  E.g.,
   134	/// `state.value = Some(42.0); state.formula = Some("=A1+1"); state.format =
   135	/// Some(FormatId::Builtin(2))` is a formula-evaluated-to-42-rendered-as-
   136	/// number-with-2-decimals cell.
   137	///
   138	/// ## Ghost-entry avoidance (V3.5.0.5 extends V3.4.0.X MEDIUM-1)
   139	///
   140	/// When ALL THREE fields are `None` after an op, the cache key is
   141	/// REMOVED entirely (not left as an empty `CellState`).  Pre-V3.5.0.5
   142	/// this rule covered (value, formula); V3.5.0.5 extends it to include
   143	/// format -- otherwise a `SetCellFormat { id: None }` on a never-written
   144	/// cell would leave a phantom cache entry that surfaces in
   145	/// `list_sheets_from_cache`.
   146	#[derive(Clone, Debug, Default, PartialEq)]
   147	pub struct CellState {
   148	    pub value: Option<CellWireValue>,
   149	    pub formula: Option<String>,
   150	    pub format: Option<FormatId>,
   151	}
   152	
   153	/// **Phase 5.7 V3.4.0.X HIGH-1 + MEDIUM-1 closure (2026-05-24)**: internal
   154	/// representation of a single cache mutation extracted from an `Op`.
   155	///
