   188	    /// into `format_table_cache` IF the id is not already present
   189	    /// (first-write-wins).
   190	    ///
   191	    /// **V3.6.0.X audit-of-D2 closure (2026-05-23,
   192	    /// CONVERGENT-HIGH-1)**: the cache walker uses `entry().or_insert`
   193	    /// (first-write-wins) to mirror `FormatTable::register_at`'s
   194	    /// `IdCollision` rejection semantic at the cache layer.  Pre-
   195	    /// closure the walker used `.insert(id, string)` (LWW-by-iteration)
   196	    /// which CONTRADICTED the V3.6.0.1 plan body § D2 line 133 locked
   197	    /// decision: "cache walker treats the second registration as a
   198	    /// no-op".  Post-closure: cache and Workbook agree on the
   199	    /// first-iterated string for any concurrent same-id-different-
   200	    /// string scenario.  See `format_table_cache` field docstring
   201	    /// for cross-peer convergence properties.
   202	    ///
   203	    /// **V3.6.0.X audit-of-D2 closure (CONVERGENT-MED-2)**: only
   204	    /// `FormatId::Custom` effects reach this variant -- `Builtin`
   205	    /// payloads are dropped at `collect_cache_effects` (the cache
   206	    /// holds "ONLY Custom format registrations" per the field
   207	    /// docstring; Workbook-side replay still accepts in-range
   208	    /// Builtin Op::RegisterFormat as Phase 4.6 D-1 semantic, deferred
   209	    /// to V3.7+).
   210	    ///
   211	    /// `string` uses `Arc<str>` for cheap clones across the walker
   212	    /// (collect_cache_effects -> apply_cache_effect).
   213	    RegisterFormat { id: FormatId, string: Arc<str> },
   214	}
   215	
   216	/// **Phase 5.7 V3.6.0.4 D3 (2026-05-23) -- bundle the 5 cache-walker
   217	/// buckets into one struct.**
   218	///
   219	/// Pre-D3 the 3 buckets (`snapshot`, `tombstones`, `format_cache`)
   220	/// were individual `&mut HashMap<...>` parameters threaded through
   221	/// `apply_cache_effect`'s signature.  V3.6.0.X audit-of-D2 Opus
   222	/// Lane B LOW-1 flagged the linear signature growth as a refactor
   223	/// risk: every new cache bucket added a parameter at the helper +
   224	/// every caller; forgetting one silently produced state-divergence
   225	/// bugs the type system didn't catch.  V3.6.0.4 D3 adds 2 more
   226	/// buckets (`cell_op_index` + `sheet_op_index` for
   227	/// O(ops-for-this-cell) `invalidate_cell`), which would have made
   228	/// the helper a 6-param call.  This struct bundles them via mutable
   229	/// references at the call site.
   230	///
   231	/// **Buckets** (in walker-mutation order):
   232	/// - `snapshot`: per-cell `CellState` (value / formula / format).
   233	/// - `tombstones`: u16 sheet ids that have been `Op::RemoveSheet`'d.
   234	/// - `format_cache`: session-wide `FormatId -> Arc<str>` registry
   235	///   (Custom registrations from `Op::RegisterFormat`).
   236	/// - `cell_op_index` **V3.6.0.4 D3**: cell coord -> sorted op-log
   237	///   indices that touch this cell.  Maintained per cell-keyed
   238	///   effect's key in `apply_cache_effect`.  Drives
   239	///   `invalidate_cell`'s O(k) walk where k = entries for the target
   240	///   cell (typically 1-3 for the LWW happy path).
   241	/// - `sheet_op_index` **V3.6.0.4 D3**: sheet id -> sorted op-log
   242	///   indices where `Op::RemoveSheet` targeted this sheet.
   243	///   `invalidate_cell` consults both `cell_op_index[(s,r,c)]` AND
   244	///   `sheet_op_index[s]` (the latter is typically 0 or 1 entry per
   245	///   sheet) to find every effect relevant to the target cell.
   246	///
   247	/// **Rule 4 trigger**: composition of 5 `&mut HashMap<K, V>`
   248	/// references.  Each `HashMap<K, V>` (with K, V Send+Sync) is itself
   249	/// Send+Sync; `&mut T` inherits Send+Sync when T does.  All 5
   250	/// keys/values are primitives or Send+Sync types covered by prior
   251	/// per-field walks (`FormatId`, `(u16, u32, u32)`, `u16`,
   252	/// `CellState`, `Arc<str>`, `Vec<usize>`).  **0 new triggers;
   253	/// arc terminus stays at 6.**
   254	struct CacheBuckets<'a> {
   255	    snapshot: &'a mut HashMap<(u16, u32, u32), CellState>,
   256	    tombstones: &'a mut HashSet<u16>,
   257	    format_cache: &'a mut HashMap<FormatId, Arc<str>>,
   258	    cell_op_index: &'a mut HashMap<(u16, u32, u32), Vec<usize>>,
   259	    sheet_op_index: &'a mut HashMap<u16, Vec<usize>>,
   260	}

