     1	//! The `Op` enum — the engine's mutation vocabulary for the op log.
     2	//!
     3	//! Phase 2A.3.a (2026-05-12): minimum producer set covering everything
     4	//! `WorkbookRuntime` and `WorkbookTransaction` can mutate through their
     5	//! public API. Future variants (sheet renames, sheet deletes, formatting
     6	//! changes) land alongside the API additions that produce them.
     7	//!
     8	//! Each variant mirrors a `Workbook` mutation method one-to-one:
     9	//!
    10	//! | `Op` variant         | Replays to                                       |
    11	//! |----------------------|--------------------------------------------------|
    12	//! | `PutValue`           | `Workbook::put_at`                               |
    13	//! | `PutFormula`         | `Workbook::put_formula`                          |
    14	//! | `ClearFormula`       | `Workbook::clear_formula`                        |
    15	//! | `SetName`            | `Workbook::set_name`                             |
    16	//! | `AddSheet`           | `Workbook::add_sheet_with_chunk_rows`            |
    17	//! | `RegisterFormat`     | `FormatTable::register_at` (W5-80)               |
    18	//! | `SetCellFormat`      | `CellFormatOverlay::set` / `::clear` (W5-80)     |
    19	//! | `BatchCommit`        | (recursive — applies each inner op in order)     |
    20	//! | `RenameSheet`        | `Workbook::rename_sheet` (Phase 4.6.C / 5.3 step 3) |
    21	//! | `RemoveSheet`        | `Workbook::remove_sheet` (V3.5.0.3b tombstone)   |
    22	//! | `MoveSheet`          | `Workbook::move_sheet` (V3.5.0.3c display-order overlay) |
    23	//! | `SetReferenceMode`   | `Workbook::set_reference_mode` (W5-146 Phase 4.9.J) |
    24	//! | `SetLocale`          | `Workbook::set_locale` (W5-146 Phase 4.9.J)      |
    25	//! | `SetDateSystem`      | `Workbook::set_date_system` (V3.6.0.X audit-of-D4 CONVERGENT-HIGH-1 closure) |
    26	//!
    27	//! ## Wire format choices
    28	//!
    29	//! - `Arc<str>` is NOT used in wire fields. `serde` without the `rc`
    30	//!   feature can't deserialize `Arc<str>` directly. We store `String` on
    31	//!   the wire and convert at the replay boundary. Cleaner separation: the
    32	//!   wire format owns its strings; the runtime types share via Arc once
    33	//!   inside the workbook.
    34	//! - `ValueWire` and `NamedTargetWire` are reused from
    35	//!   `ql_io::qbook_format` (Phase 2A.8 shipped them). Sharing the
    36	//!   serialization vocabulary across the engine's three persistence
    37	//!   surfaces (qbook envelope, qbook JSONL, op log) prevents wire-format
    38	//!   drift.
